        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "5b8946d9-383a-31db-97e0-1ed34ac70aae",
                "word": "pusillanime",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "d63189e5-132e-41b3-9335-557d2d07fa89",
                        "entry_id": "5b8946d9-383a-31db-97e0-1ed34ac70aae",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "masculine",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "pusillanimes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bfa8a10e-92e4-3000-bd36-dd40b7082948",
                        "entry_id": "5b8946d9-383a-31db-97e0-1ed34ac70aae",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui manque de courage, de caractère ; qui fuit les responsabilités."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "literary"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6cbe7003-4aca-4424-807f-d8349c4519f0",
                                "sense_id": "bfa8a10e-92e4-3000-bd36-dd40b7082948",
                                "text": "Je hais ces cœurs pusillanimes qui, pour trop prévoir les suites des choses, n’osent rien entreprendre."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d4472f9b-19f6-4175-9ff0-d6627e15e1b0",
                                "sense_id": "bfa8a10e-92e4-3000-bd36-dd40b7082948",
                                "text": "Dans tout ce qu'on entreprend, il faut donner les deux tiers à la raison, et l'autre tiers au hasard. Augmentez la première fraction, et vous serez pusillanime. Augmentez la seconde, vous serez téméraire."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0710ff10-cce4-4bf4-9b0e-9686e4b91d6f",
                                "sense_id": "bfa8a10e-92e4-3000-bd36-dd40b7082948",
                                "text": "Un semi-scepticisme est la marque d’un esprit faible ; il décèle un raisonneur pusillanime, qui se laisse effrayer par les conséquences ; […]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "19acd3d9-1d7f-46fa-b3b2-4fd981fd8974",
                                "sense_id": "bfa8a10e-92e4-3000-bd36-dd40b7082948",
                                "text": "Le commandant du vaisseau le Amherst, qui vient de parcourir leurs côtes, abordant et débarquant malgré eux où bon lui semblait, nous les fait voir aussi pusillanimes, aussi menteurs, aussi méprisables que possible."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d02fcf7b-267b-459b-9d64-d0bf25645eee",
                                "sense_id": "bfa8a10e-92e4-3000-bd36-dd40b7082948",
                                "text": "Si j’avais voyagé en diligence, je les aurais pris aisément pour des brigands, bien que, m’a-t-on dit, ils ne fassent jamais de mal à personne ; au contraire, ils sont plutôt pusillanimes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f8bab32d-16f8-4df1-b5d9-660991097796",
                                "sense_id": "bfa8a10e-92e4-3000-bd36-dd40b7082948",
                                "text": "Peut-être qu'après tout il ne faisait que rendre service à ce pauvre Mr Dowes, pusillanime et froussard."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1aaac6a4-72b4-433a-8531-da56851002ab",
                                "sense_id": "bfa8a10e-92e4-3000-bd36-dd40b7082948",
                                "text": "Ce que ne montre pas la sculpture c’est la relation acrimonieuse entre les deux hommes : Tycho le Danois riche, dodu, arrogant avec ses vêtements extravagants et son nez métallique ; Kepler l’Allemand pusillanime, renfermé, mystique."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "acbff354-00fb-431e-bc28-61d295566e5d",
                        "source_entry_id": "5b8946d9-383a-31db-97e0-1ed34ac70aae",
                        "source_sense_id": "bfa8a10e-92e4-3000-bd36-dd40b7082948",
                        "target_lang_word": "kleinmütig",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "kleinmütig",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d0ff7de9-c0ac-3253-b9d6-efe9b0b9775d",
                                        "entry_id": "fa408316-3726-3534-8f1f-ebd8ae22e890",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "mutlos, verzagt, ohne Selbstvertrauen, ohne Entschlusskraft"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "literary"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bceb4787-165a-464b-bd32-f82847633f25",
                                                "sense_id": "d0ff7de9-c0ac-3253-b9d6-efe9b0b9775d",
                                                "text": "„Moritz Wiggers versuchte zwar noch eine Aufhebung des Tagungsverbots zu erreichen, scheiterte aber an der kleinmütigen Haltung einiger Abgeordneter und der fehlenden Beschlussfähigkeit.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "183691ea-c09c-4c87-ae77-b1aeaeeff4d5",
                                                "sense_id": "d0ff7de9-c0ac-3253-b9d6-efe9b0b9775d",
                                                "text": "„Der öffentlichen Beschallung entnehme ich, dass wir nicht kleinmütig werden sollen, nur wegen der einen oder anderen Bedrohung, die zwischendurch kurz aufblitzt.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "463b70ac-800f-417e-8d9e-cb33f815c846",
                        "source_entry_id": "5b8946d9-383a-31db-97e0-1ed34ac70aae",
                        "source_sense_id": "bfa8a10e-92e4-3000-bd36-dd40b7082948",
                        "target_lang_word": "pusillanimous",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "pusillanimous",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5d93eab2-49d1-39d3-9ded-33fdea421afb",
                                        "entry_id": "ffcdd75b-c438-31a5-804f-d02a2ef4d7a0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Showing ignoble cowardice, or contemptible timidity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c4400663-6656-4cf9-afd3-db11644c3db7",
                                                "sense_id": "5d93eab2-49d1-39d3-9ded-33fdea421afb",
                                                "text": "The soldier deserted his troop in a pusillanimous manner."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5b045b56-ec2e-4a75-b794-c32845686b44",
                                                "sense_id": "5d93eab2-49d1-39d3-9ded-33fdea421afb",
                                                "text": "Therefore, the wise thing is for us diligently to train ourselves to lie thoughtfully, judiciously; to lie with a good object, and not an evil one; to lie for others' advantage, and not our own; to lie healingly, charitably, humanely, not cruelly, hurtfully, maliciously; to lie gracefully and graciously, not awkwardly and clumsily; to lie firmly, frankly, squarely, with head erect, not haltingly, tortuously, with pusillanimous mien, as being ashamed of our high calling."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "08013db7-5a59-4e41-a625-267c73df315c",
                                                "sense_id": "5d93eab2-49d1-39d3-9ded-33fdea421afb",
                                                "text": "(Aaron Burr and Andrew Jackson ride together in Tennessee; Burr narrates): Jackson shouted at me his view of the duel. \"Never read such a damned lot of nonsense as the press has been writing! All that hypocritical caterwauling for that Creole bastard (referring to Alexander Hamilton) who fought you of his own free will, just like a gentleman which he wasn't, if you'll forgive me, Colonel! I know you couldn't have met him unless you thought he was one, but he was not, Sir. He was the worst man in this union, as you, Sir, are the best. The best, and that goes for that pusillanimous spotted caitiff of a president (referring to Thomas Jefferson) we got."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "882f957c-85a8-4e52-96a4-7d6183690028",
                                                "sense_id": "5d93eab2-49d1-39d3-9ded-33fdea421afb",
                                                "text": "Octavian, by contrast, was pusillanimous in battle ... but proved himself extremely adept in the political arena"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a243d173-9171-4d1c-9ab8-460acf813583",
                        "source_entry_id": "5b8946d9-383a-31db-97e0-1ed34ac70aae",
